  "body": "  (34 pts.) Prove both of the following. Note that adding two rational numbers together results in a rational number (i.e. the set of rational numbers is closed under addition) and multiplying two rational numbers results in a rational number (i.e. the set of rational numbers is closed under multiplication). However, adding or multiplying two irrational numbers may not result in an irrational number (e.g. and ). Make sure to state the theorems you prove as mathematical statements (not commands).   Suppose that is a nonzero rational number and is an irrational number (i.e. a real number that is not a rational number). Prove that is an irrational number.    Let be a real number, and let be an irrational number. Prove that either or is an irrational number.      "
