  "body": " Resources for 4\/12    For the content of this class, you will be expected to be able to do the following:     State and apply the definition of a digraph .    Describe basic terminology related to digraphs, including vertex, arc, walk, path, cycle, trail , and circuit .    Use Dijkstra's Algorithm or the Improved Dijkstra's Algorithm to find shortest paths between vertices in digraphs.      Video & Activities for Directed Graphs  Below is a YouTube video on directed graphs , also known as digraphs . It is followed by a link to a set of activities that we will be working on in class. Please watch the video and do as many of the activities as you can before class.    Digraphs & Shortest Path Algorithms (No Quiz)     graph={1:[2,5],2:[3],3:[4],4:[5]}  labels={1:'a',2:'b',3:'c',4:'d',5:'e',6:'f',7:'g'}           4  5  2  1  10  3  6  4  2  2  4  8       Use either Dijkstra's or Improved Dijkstra's Algorithm on the weighted digraph above to determine the distance between and the other vertices.     Optional Reading   Digraphs and Shortest Paths    "
